{"route":"/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Using Bootstrap with AI","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn about Bootstrap’s machine-readable docs and skills files for working with LLMs and agentic developer tools."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap ships resources built for large language models and AI-powered coding tools: machine-readable documentation you can feed to an LLM, and a set of agent skills that walk agents through common Bootstrap tasks step by step."},{"id":"llm-ready-docs","type":"heading","en":"LLM-ready docs","level":2},{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Our docs are available in a machine-readable format, following the <a href=\"https://llmstxt.org/\">llms.txt</a> convention."},{"id":"llm-ready-docs--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"File"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Link"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>llms.txt</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"A curated index of every documentation page with links and descriptions."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/llms.txt\">/llms.txt</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>llms-full.txt</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"The full text of the documentation concatenated into a single file for direct ingestion."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"llm-ready-docs--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/llms-full.txt\">/llms-full.txt</a>"}]}]}]},{"id":"skills","type":"heading","en":"Skills","level":2},{"id":"skills--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install every Bootstrap skill into your coding agent:"},{"id":"skills--code-1","type":"code","value":"npx skills add twbs/bootstrap","language":""},{"id":"skills--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The Skills CLI copies each <code>SKILL.md</code> from our repository into your agent. <a href=\"https://skills.sh/\">skills.sh</a> lists the package after people run that command. There is no submit form."},{"id":"skills--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap also ships the same <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills\">agent skills</a> in the <code>skills/</code> directory of our repository. Each skill is a focused, step-by-step playbook for one Bootstrap task, from migrating a project or setting up a new build to authoring a component and customizing our color system."},{"id":"skills--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"To use one without the CLI, point your agent at the relevant <code>SKILL.md</code> file and describe what you want to do. The skill’s <code>description</code> field tells the agent when it applies, and its steps keep the agent aligned with our official guidance. Always review an agent’s changes against the matching documentation."},{"id":"skills--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","scope":"col","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Skill"}]},{"type":"th","scope":"col","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"Description"}]},{"type":"th","scope":"col","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"Guide"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-v4-v6-migration\"><code>bootstrap-v4-v6-migration</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"Migrate a project from Bootstrap 4 to Bootstrap 6. Use when upgrading from Bootstrap 4, jumping two major versions, or updating v4 class names, data attributes, forms, and JavaScript across the v4-to-v5 and v5-to-v6 steps."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/migration\">Migration</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-v5-v6-migration\"><code>bootstrap-v5-v6-migration</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"Migrate projects from Bootstrap 5 to Bootstrap 6. Use when upgrading from Bootstrap 5, migrating v5 to v6, or updating v5 class names, components, Sass, or JavaScript to the latest version. For Bootstrap 4 projects, start with the v4-to-v6 migration skill instead."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/migration\">Migration</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-v6-install\"><code>bootstrap-v6-install</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"Add Bootstrap 6 to a project and set it up for local development. Use when installing Bootstrap, adding Bootstrap to a new or existing project, or setting up Bootstrap&#39;s CSS and JavaScript via CDN or a package manager."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install\">Install Bootstrap</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-17","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-npm\"><code>bootstrap-npm</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-18","type":"paragraph","en":"Build a Bootstrap 6 starter project using just npm and command-line tools (no bundler). Use when setting up Bootstrap with npm, compiling Bootstrap&#39;s Sass to CSS from the command line, or creating an npm-based Bootstrap project."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-19","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/npm\">Bootstrap and npm</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-20","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-webpack\"><code>bootstrap-webpack</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-21","type":"paragraph","en":"Include and bundle Bootstrap 6&#39;s CSS and JavaScript in a project using Webpack. Use when setting up Bootstrap with Webpack, configuring Webpack loaders for Bootstrap&#39;s Sass and JS, or creating a Webpack-based Bootstrap project."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-22","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/webpack\">Bootstrap and Webpack</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-23","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-parcel\"><code>bootstrap-parcel</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-24","type":"paragraph","en":"Include and bundle Bootstrap 6&#39;s CSS and JavaScript in a project using Parcel. Use when setting up Bootstrap with Parcel, bundling Bootstrap&#39;s Sass and JS through Parcel, or creating a Parcel-based Bootstrap project."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-25","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/parcel\">Bootstrap and Parcel</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-26","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-vite\"><code>bootstrap-vite</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-27","type":"paragraph","en":"Include and bundle Bootstrap 6&#39;s CSS and JavaScript in a project using Vite. Use when setting up Bootstrap with Vite, bundling Bootstrap&#39;s Sass and JS through Vite, or creating a Vite-based Bootstrap project."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-28","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/guides/vite\">Bootstrap and Vite</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-29","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-component\"><code>bootstrap-component</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-30","type":"paragraph","en":"Build a Bootstrap 6 component&#39;s CSS and markup. Use when creating a new component, adding modifier or variant classes, or authoring component styles with Bootstrap&#39;s Sass token maps and theme overrides."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-31","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/components\">Components</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-32","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-component-js\"><code>bootstrap-component-js</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-33","type":"paragraph","en":"Add JavaScript behavior to a Bootstrap 6 component. Use when writing a component&#39;s TypeScript source, extending BaseComponent, wiring the data API, adding events or config options, or integrating Floating UI or a third-party library."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-34","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript\">JavaScript</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-35","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-color-system\"><code>bootstrap-color-system</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-36","type":"paragraph","en":"Work with Bootstrap 6&#39;s color system in Sass and CSS. Use when customizing colors, adding or overriding theme colors, working with color modes, or using the color scales, semantic tokens, and theme classes."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-37","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/customize/color\">Color</a>"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-38","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/tree/main/skills/bootstrap-utility-api\"><code>bootstrap-utility-api</code></a>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-39","type":"paragraph","en":"Use, extend, and customize Bootstrap 6&#39;s utility API. Use when adding a custom utility class, modifying or removing Bootstrap&#39;s default utilities, enabling responsive or state variants, or trimming the generated utility CSS."}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"skills--paragraph-40","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/api\">Utility API</a>"}]}]}]}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.